From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Send every bit of the chosen mode to the receiver

The descriptor sent to the receiver in M4 names the chosen mode as one bit of
a 32-bit table mask, but the masks were held in 16-bit variables. A mode from
bit 16 up, 1080p24 in the CEA table (patch 0025) or any of its 4K modes, was
sent as no mode at all.

diff -ruN a/src/wfd/wfd-video-codec.c b/src/wfd/wfd-video-codec.c
--- a/src/wfd/wfd-video-codec.c
+++ b/src/wfd/wfd-video-codec.c
@@ -468,7 +468,7 @@
 gchar *
 wfd_video_codec_get_descriptor_for_resolution (WfdVideoCodec *self, const WfdResolution *resolution)
 {
-  guint16 cae_sup, vesa_sup, hh_sup;
+  guint32 cae_sup, vesa_sup, hh_sup;
   guint32 slice_enc_params;
   guint8 frame_rate_ctrl_sup;
 
